Package: nlkernel
Title: Non linear kernels for Genomic Prediction with Cross Validation
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Wanessa", "Paiva", , "wwanessa13@hotmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: This package provides a unified framework for genomic prediction using kernel-based methods within the RKHS paradigm implemented in BGLR. It includes functions for fitting and evaluating Gaussian, Bessel, Laplace, Polynomial, and GBLUP models, as well as dimensionality reduction approaches such as PCA and kernel PCA (KPCA). The package supports flexible hyperparameter tuning, automatic selection of principal components based on explained variance thresholds, and k-fold cross-validation for robust model assessment. It also allows combining multiple kernels in a single model. Results are returned in a structured format with prediction outputs and can be optionally exported for downstream analysis.
